-- TYPICALLY has no counterpart in DMN, and the export says so.
--
-- A DMN inputData, a BKM parameter and a record's itemComponent carry no
-- default: an evaluation that leaves one out gets `null` on Camunda 8 and a
-- model error on KIE (jl4/tests-cli/fixtures/dmn-null-probe/null-absent.dmn
-- measured both). Rewriting every read as `if x = null then d else x` would
-- change what each decision says and would not help KIE at all, so the exporter
-- does not map a default; it reports each one as a D-TYPICALLY note
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC ruling T5). One of each place a TYPICALLY can
-- sit: a section GIVEN, a rule's own GIVEN, and a record field; plus a rule's
-- GIVEN that is the input column of a decision table, the one shape dmn-md can
-- draw.
--
-- The cases in defaults.cases.json supply every input, which is all a DMN
-- evaluation can honestly be asked.

DECLARE Config HAS
    timeout IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 30
    retries IS A NUMBER

§ `Capacity`
    GIVEN `has capacity` IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY TRUE

@export Whether the person may contract
GIVEN `is adult` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`may contract` MEANS `has capacity` AND `is adult`

@export The fee for a rate
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee` rate base MEANS base TIMES rate

@export The budget for a configuration
GIVEN c IS A Config
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the budget` c MEANS (c's timeout) TIMES (c's retries)

@export The band for an income
GIVEN income IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 50000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the band` income MEANS
    BRANCH
      IF income AT LEAST 100000 THEN 3
      IF income AT LEAST 50000 THEN 2
      OTHERWISE 1
